[{:db/id 17592186129213 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129640 :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186127321 :answer-field/correct 17592186127325 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6" :question/id #uuid "e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-97060" :question/problem "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-14b5fd09-d567-55da-9493-1ac629b8d62a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-14b5fd09-d567-55da-9493-1ac629b8d62a" :answer-field/id #uuid "14b5fd09-d567-55da-9493-1ac629b8d62a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2090546c-8891-5b10-af98-9204905ac08a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-27f9e9c7-23c3-5ee6-82bd-1ed602f60cb6" "answer-2090546c-8891-5b10-af98-9204905ac08a" "answer-12910645-377d-54ef-bc0b-422296caf8f8" "answer-39e6d5c4-ef80-5978-98b7-b10c7c9e811a" "answer-da77cae2-0a6d-576c-9bbf-669849034a2f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27f9e9c7-23c3-5ee6-82bd-1ed602f60cb6" :answer/id #uuid "27f9e9c7-23c3-5ee6-82bd-1ed602f60cb6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2090546c-8891-5b10-af98-9204905ac08a" :answer/id #uuid "2090546c-8891-5b10-af98-9204905ac08a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12910645-377d-54ef-bc0b-422296caf8f8" :answer/id #uuid "12910645-377d-54ef-bc0b-422296caf8f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39e6d5c4-ef80-5978-98b7-b10c7c9e811a" :answer/id #uuid "39e6d5c4-ef80-5978-98b7-b10c7c9e811a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da77cae2-0a6d-576c-9bbf-669849034a2f" :answer/id #uuid "da77cae2-0a6d-576c-9bbf-669849034a2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2" :question/id #uuid "662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97118" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-32c807d8-09ff-597f-a633-55d26150ec43"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-32c807d8-09ff-597f-a633-55d26150ec43" :answer-field/id #uuid "32c807d8-09ff-597f-a633-55d26150ec43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f47a664-a9ad-5deb-90c8-17a7a38adab0" "answer-d0704113-7386-54ca-ad0c-7578acd9ac62" "answer-0b6934d8-eaf0-5f13-b06a-71ac2a0dc0af" "answer-5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" "answer-dc81c6b4-cc09-56a5-916c-e323cc4197ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f47a664-a9ad-5deb-90c8-17a7a38adab0" :answer/id #uuid "8f47a664-a9ad-5deb-90c8-17a7a38adab0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0704113-7386-54ca-ad0c-7578acd9ac62" :answer/id #uuid "d0704113-7386-54ca-ad0c-7578acd9ac62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -11 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b6934d8-eaf0-5f13-b06a-71ac2a0dc0af" :answer/id #uuid "0b6934d8-eaf0-5f13-b06a-71ac2a0dc0af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer/id #uuid "5c9c3643-ad71-51e0-bd19-40d272c2cabe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc81c6b4-cc09-56a5-916c-e323cc4197ee" :answer/id #uuid "dc81c6b4-cc09-56a5-916c-e323cc4197ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7afd5a54-c223-5e70-9582-9406545b2d06"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7afd5a54-c223-5e70-9582-9406545b2d06" :question/id #uuid "7afd5a54-c223-5e70-9582-9406545b2d06" :question/math-academy-id "q-97279" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ 7 & 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2c3a3177-a079-5cdb-a624-7225c5f182a3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2c3a3177-a079-5cdb-a624-7225c5f182a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c3a3177-a079-5cdb-a624-7225c5f182a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-248c47da-3dc5-5333-809d-acf62be00f30" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd75b99f-ca84-5149-9b32-732c0d712c4b" "answer-7d527527-44f7-5758-b7fd-4c2cd30a0912" "answer-248c47da-3dc5-5333-809d-acf62be00f30" "answer-c7cdd80b-8123-585f-9ada-143e7f38d137" "answer-094350f2-e017-53e0-b0e9-5075268dbe4d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd75b99f-ca84-5149-9b32-732c0d712c4b" :answer/id #uuid "cd75b99f-ca84-5149-9b32-732c0d712c4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -18 \\\\ -9 & -16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d527527-44f7-5758-b7fd-4c2cd30a0912" :answer/id #uuid "7d527527-44f7-5758-b7fd-4c2cd30a0912" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-248c47da-3dc5-5333-809d-acf62be00f30" :answer/id #uuid "248c47da-3dc5-5333-809d-acf62be00f30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -12 \\\\ 7 & 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7cdd80b-8123-585f-9ada-143e7f38d137" :answer/id #uuid "c7cdd80b-8123-585f-9ada-143e7f38d137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-094350f2-e017-53e0-b0e9-5075268dbe4d" :answer/id #uuid "094350f2-e017-53e0-b0e9-5075268dbe4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" :question/id #uuid "426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140453" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b" :answer-field/id #uuid "80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6431b86f-886e-5d1c-a26b-505391b5eaa1" "answer-b7bd80ae-8e71-5474-9567-c47f73ef5af4" "answer-5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" "answer-9029cfa0-da2b-5680-a6e9-bd10f503ed2f" "answer-3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6431b86f-886e-5d1c-a26b-505391b5eaa1" :answer/id #uuid "6431b86f-886e-5d1c-a26b-505391b5eaa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ 14 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7bd80ae-8e71-5474-9567-c47f73ef5af4" :answer/id #uuid "b7bd80ae-8e71-5474-9567-c47f73ef5af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/id #uuid "5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9029cfa0-da2b-5680-a6e9-bd10f503ed2f" :answer/id #uuid "9029cfa0-da2b-5680-a6e9-bd10f503ed2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af" :answer/id #uuid "3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a3e8a2c7-af14-540f-a7b1-76dc269d676b" :activity/id #uuid "a3e8a2c7-af14-540f-a7b1-76dc269d676b" :activity/title "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050324 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" "step-9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" "step-0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" "step-49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" "step-bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51"] :activity/first-step "step-1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" :step/id #uuid "1b0f643e-dd6c-5eaf-875c-1b54d4c6e171" :step/content 17592186129640 :step/next "step-9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" :step/id #uuid "9a18e940-4aa2-5db0-8cbe-98d6ec06c6cd" :step/content "question-e737a421-d643-51f0-9d67-b9556fcc15c6" :step/next "step-0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" :step/id #uuid "0b2e1e0a-a93e-5b2b-ba4a-b6011da00e9b" :step/content "question-662e0d41-a6b8-58b3-ad4a-e835c48f17e2" :step/next "step-49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" :step/id #uuid "49084fac-fe76-5f2f-8b13-058b89e81921" :step/content "question-7afd5a54-c223-5e70-9582-9406545b2d06" :step/next "step-bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51" :step/id #uuid "bf368b08-5b21-5ea2-9201-b8d34ec52b51" :step/content "question-426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
